WEBVTT

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:05.750
Hey, Kojima! I'm gonna be swimming in chocolate today,
so I'll share mine if you don't get any.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.750
Whatever, two girls already gave me some!

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.420
Good morning!

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:08.420
Morning.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.790
Yeah, right!

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.380
Valentine's Day has come, huh?

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.790
I'm super nervous.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.000
Me too!

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.830
February 14th.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.460
I have no doubt that Takagi-san will once again

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.790
take advantage of all the excitement around
this day to tease me somehow.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.420
But...

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.290
I'm not gonna fall for any of her tricks!

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.170
Called it!

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.540
Takagi-san put 3 gifts in my shoe locker, right off the bat.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.630
But... I know this is only the beginning.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.500
They've gotta be rigged like this.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.080
Or maybe like this.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.540
Or even like this.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.500
I already know what to expect!

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.630
Okay! Bring it on!

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:54.380
<b>FOR SENPAI</b>

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.210
She made them look awfully legit...

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:53.920
"Senpai"?

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:56.830
What's that mean?

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.960
<b>FOR SENPAI</b>

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:01.080
I totally don't know where Takagi-san
is going with all this...

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.080
<b>FOR SENPAI</b>

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:07.380
Actually, none of this looks like Takagi-san's handwriting.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.830
<b>Dear Senpai,</b>

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.830
<b>I fell in love with you because of Culture Fest</b>

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.830
<b>Please accept this gift</b>

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.830
"Dear Senpai, I fell in love with you
because of culture fest..."

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.750
Wha?!

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:17.960
N-no way...

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.920
So these aren't from Takagi-san,
but from girls in the grade below me?!

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.630
And there's 3 of them?!

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:59.460
<b>February 14th</b>

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.540
February 14th.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.420
Real... quietly...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.750
Good morning, Nishikata.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.330
G'morning, Takagi-san!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.830
Y-you're here, uh, really early today.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.540
Yeah, I had something to do.
So I rode to school on my bike.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.130
Oh yeah?

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:29.420
I gotta make sure Takagi-san
doesn't ask me about the chocolate.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.540
Hey, Nishikata?

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.790
What holiday is it today?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.170
Keep it together!

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:40.000
I knew that Takagi-san was going to tease me
about Valentine's Day like this,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.170
because I totally foresaw it coming yesterday!

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:47.630
I already thought up the best reply for this situation!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.250
Ah, today is February 14th.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.330
National dried sardine day.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:58.880
Can you figure out why, Takagi-san?
Try writing out the numbers 2, 1, 4 on the board.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.210
Get it?

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:09.290
If you think of the 1 as a dash,
then it spells "niboshi" or "dried sardines".

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.920
It's a play on words using numbers, right?

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.670
A little far-fetched, though.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.880
Sure, but it's a real thing people celebrate!

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:18.330
By the way, Nishikata.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.080
Are you trying to hide something right now?

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.670
Nope! Not at all!

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.880
Nothing gets by Takagi-san. She's too sharp!

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.210
I've gotta find a way to keep her
from changing the subject.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.080
I know!

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:36.500
In honor of national dried sardine day, why don't
we try having a conversation with only numbers?

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.830
Converse with numbers?

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.500
Yep. Uh, I'll start so you can get the idea.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.460
If you interpret it wrong, you lose.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.170
Is it "good morning"?

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.080
That was quick!

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.500
So? Did I get it right?

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.750
I guess I made that one a little too easy.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.250
Okay. It's your turn now, Takagi-san.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.330
All right.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:04.630
I'm gonna figure it out in no time flat!

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.330
"Va-len"... tine?!

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.170
Whew, it's not that.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.000
I'm finished.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.080
That's too easy! It says: "totally exposed"!

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.830
Huh?!

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:29.710
W-wait, does that mean she already knows
about me trying to hide the chocolate?!

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.040
Too bad! It says "totally clear".

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.630
I was trying to say that it's a nice day outside,
since the sky is so clear.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.170
Talking in numbers is hard, huh?

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.460
Uh, yeah.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.080
I almost had a heart attack!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.920
Your guess was only a little off,
but that still means you lose the contest, right?

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:51.540
Uh, yeah.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.170
I'm glad I was wrong!

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.080
Okay, then you have a penalty.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.000
What should I make you do?

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:03.170
Thinking about it, why am I so desperate to hide
the fact that some girls gave me chocolate, anyway?

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.380
Yeah, it makes no sense!

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.630
I should just come right out and say: "some girls
in the grade below us gave me chocolate!"

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.080
I've got it!

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.330
Today's homework.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:14.830
Just let me see your answers for a minute.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.330
Homework...?

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:19.540
Yep.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.670
There's one problem that I want
to double check my answer.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.960
Really? Well, I don't mind.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.710
That's the penalty for me losing?

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.290
How weird, Takagi-san never asks to see my homework...

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:35.750
If I open my bag, the chocolate will be in full view!

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:37.830
Is there a problem?

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:42.710
Okay, I'm just going to come clean with Takagi-san.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:46.750
She might even help me figure out
how I should respond to them...

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:48.960
Takagi-san?

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.210
Actually...

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.580
Forget it.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.000
Huh?

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.750
It's okay. I think my answer is right.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.830
Oh, I see.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.540
I missed my chance to bring it up...

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.750
But I don't understand. Takagi-san is normally way
more relentless when she's teasing me.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.380
It feels like she would just have a good laugh
if she found the chocolate...

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.500
Merry Valentine!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:24.880
Merry Valey.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.460
Where'd you come up with that greeting?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:31.170
Ya know, I've been thinking lately that
Valentine's Day is just as fun as Christmas is!

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:34.960
So in that spirit, here's a gift from Santa Mina!

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:38.500
I went the extra mile to make
something fancy for you two this year.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:39.710
Here!

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:49.790
The bonds of our friendship are so strong that they're
way tougher than any regular bar of chocolate!

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:52.080
That was my inspiration for making these!

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:55.000
Wow, Mina! It's touching to know how much you care.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:56.500
Okay, but...

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.540
Those "bonds of friendship" have...

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.790
melted into a gooey mess.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.130
Wha?!

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.830
H-how did that happen?

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.500
I even put them in the fridge to keep them safe!

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.250
I'm betting this is to blame.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.710
Ahhh!

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.880
I thought I dropped that somewhere this morning,
but that's where it was?!

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:16.830
A hand-warmer, huh?

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.040
I worked so hard on them...

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:22.130
Uh, it's okay! Don't cry!

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:27.500
I actually think it looks pretty cool! Like we all
combined into one with the power of friendship!

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:28.960
I'm sure it tastes great.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.170
Really?

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:32.500
Yes, really.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:34.250
Here, I also have something for you.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:36.080
It's not homemade or anything, but...

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:47.670
It's just like they say, three heads
are better than a home run!

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.670
Merry Valey.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:06.920
Nakai-kun, this is for you!

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.330
Whoa! Did you get me chocolate?!

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.830
Shush! You're being too loud!

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:13.920
You know Tanabe-sensei confiscates candy!

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.460
Sorry, my bad.

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:17.580
Valentine's... huh?

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:18.920
Don't say a word.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.290
Sorry, man.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:22.210
Hamaguchi.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.460
Chocolate. Want some?

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:28.000
Dude.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.420
Y-yeah, if it's from you.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.420
Okay then.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:34.670
Here.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:41.000
Hurry and take it before a teacher shows up.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.790
Uh, right.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.170
Thanks!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:46.670
Bye.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.670
Congrats, man.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:52.920
Guys...

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.540
This isn't homemade.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:00.420
I randomly saw her shopping yesterday.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:04.290
Hojo was buying ingredients for homemade chocolate!

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:08.210
If she's not handing out the homemade stuff now...

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.670
That means... it was only for the one she loves!

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.380
For someone... who isn't me!

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.960
Just be happy you actually got some.

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.750
I'll eat it if you're not gonna.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.420
Console me, dang it!

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:24.710
To make comparative adjectives
you add "er" at the end of the word.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:28.250
And for superlative form you add "est"
at the end of the word.

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.630
But be aware there are multiple exceptions to this.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:37.330
For example, there are some longer adjectives
that are different like "beautiful".

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.330
I wonder what's going on with her?

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:41.790
To make those comparative you have
to add "more", as in "more beautiful".

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:47.210
Then for superlative form you have
to add "most", as in "most beautiful".

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.380
Hey, Nishikata.

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.920
You're on the wrong page.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:47.710
Huh?!

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.290
This is so weird.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:11:01.170
It feels like Takagi-san is missing so many opportunities
to do her usual teasing, but with a Valentine's Day twist.

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:05.790
I'll never get the opportunity to tell her
about the chocolate like this...

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:07.920
Fine!

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.330
I'll just have to take the initiative!

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.540
Hey, Takagi-san?

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:14.710
Care for a contest?

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.040
What kind?

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:19.080
A contest to see who can make
the longer eraser rubbing!

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.580
Just like this...

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.210
You keep extending it until it breaks.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.250
The winner is whoever has the longer one.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.210
Sounds good to me.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.580
I haven't completed my training with this yet.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:37.540
I was only going to challenge her after
I broke 2.5 centimeters, but...

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:45.670
I'm going to cast my pride aside for now
and lose this one on purpose!

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:46.920
And then...

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.040
Yay! I'm the winner!

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.080
Crud! I can't believe I lost!

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:56.750
Oh well! I guess for my penalty, I'll reluctantly
share the secret that I've been keeping all morning!

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.420
Whoa! What are all those?!

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.540
And that's how it'll go.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:03.750
So, can I go first?

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:04.880
Fine with me.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:05.750
Okay.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.130
Aw man, this is so hard.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.130
I think I might lose!

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:16.750
Do your thing, Takagi-san. I know you're gonna try
and throw me off with some teasing!

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.460
Huh?

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:24.420
Nothing?

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:29.380
3.5 centimeters.

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.670
I seriously just broke my personal best?!

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:35.000
How does this happen only when I'm trying to lose?!

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.710
That's amazing. Way to go, Nishikata.

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.920
What is going on, Takagi-san?!
Why aren't you teasing me?!

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.210
It's my turn now.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:44.210
Good luck.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.830
Please! I really need you to win this!

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.710
I know you can pull it off, Takagi-san!

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:52.000
Yeah! Looking good so far, Takagi-san!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.170
Hey, Nishikata. If I win this contest...

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.460
S-s-sure, I'll do whatever you want me to!

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.330
I know, how about this?
If you win I'll tell you a secret of mine!

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:05.830
Actually, I'm just not feeling it today.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:06.790
What?!

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:11.380
The Takagi-san I know would
never give up on a contest like that!

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:14.290
Pigs must be flying outside! No, forget pigs,
I bet elephants are flying about now!

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:17.000
Don't give up, you can do better than that.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:19.250
You're the one who needs to do better.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.710
Tell me what the comparative and
superlative forms of "beautiful" are.

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:28.290
B-b-b-beautifuler! Beautifulest!

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.790
Nishikata! Learn to pay attention, already!

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:32.710
I'm sorry, sir!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.670
Get it together. This is gonna be on the test, you know!

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.210
Make sure you all review the material.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:39.750
Yes, sir!

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.250
Oh, thank god. Takagi-san's back to normal.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:49.130
Sakurai-kun was so happy when I gave it to him.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.080
Come back!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.630
Don't let them score!

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.500
Yo, let's hit up the candy store after school.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.170
Sounds good. Today's the day to treat
ourselves to a chocolate binge!

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.080
I gotta tell Takagi-san somehow...

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:03.210
Excuse me.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.750
Is Nishikata-senpai here?

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:09.880
Nishikata! You've got visitors!

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:19.540
Yes?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.710
U-uh, well, we wanted to ask about our chocolates...

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:24.960
Chocolate?!

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:26.670
That traitor!

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.920
Are you talking about these?

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:31.960
<b>FOR SENPAI</b>

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.330
Yes, those!

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.420
Thanks for giving them to me.

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:40.460
Nishikawa... those darn chocolate temptresses
have even lured you to the other side now.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:41.880
And three of them at that.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:43.830
So, after I gave it to my dad, he was like...

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:47.250
But I'm sorry! I can't accept these!

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:54.540
I'm honestly happy you feel that way, but I...

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.670
I'm real sorry about this!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.250
What a relief!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:14:59.880
Huh?

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.960
Actually, we had put them into the wrong shoe locker.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:04.710
What?

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.670
Jeez, it's all your fault for insisting
you knew which locker it was.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.330
Sorry. Turns out I was off by one row!

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.460
We're very sorry for the trouble!

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:14.960
So then...

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.790
could you go and get Shibasaki-senpai for us?

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.170
Shibasaki-senpai!

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:26.170
You were so cute playing the role
of the dog during the Culture Fest!

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.750
So, since it's Valentine's...

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.790
Please accept our chocolate!

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:30.460
Thanks!

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:34.290
Man, you should've ate all their chocolate earlier!

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:35.210
Totally.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:40.500
This is great! Now I don't have to worry
about keeping any secrets from Takagi-san.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:44.210
Wait. Where is Takagi-san, anyway?

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.920
The sky looks nice today...

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.330
Why is your mouth hanging open?

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:03.000
Hojo!

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.210
It makes you look like a scary zombie.
You should cut it out.

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.960
So, what's got you feeling down?

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:12.960
I'm not feeling down.

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:14.130
Quit lying.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:17.080
I know exactly what you look
like when you're feeling down.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.290
Just like that.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:23.130
We've known each other for practically forever.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:28.420
Ah, I know. You feel down because
you didn't get more chocolate. That right?

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.380
What about you, Hojo?

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:37.210
Did you give the guy you like your homemade chocolate?

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:38.920
Homemade?

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:40.500
You don't have to play dumb with me!

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.460
I know you made some!

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:45.290
H-how do you know about that?!

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.920
Cuz I happened to see you at
the supermarket buying the ingredients for it...

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:52.580
I...

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:54.500
burnt them.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.540
They got ruined. All of them.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:57.330
Huh?

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.920
I only took my eyes off of them for a second!

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:02.380
How does chocolate burn so quickly, anyway?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:08.750
What's your problem? Is it really so
hilarious to find out that I screwed up?

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.380
No! I'm sorry.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.710
Well, I'm glad to see you're feeling better now.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:15.500
Thanks.

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:19.330
That means... the chocolate she gave me was...

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:24.170
I expect luxury brand chocolate from you on White Day.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.170
Uh... r-right!

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:34.080
Shucks. I guess I'm not getting any
chocolate from Takagi-san this year.

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:41.540
Well, it's not like I wanted it anyway!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.330
But...

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.170
Huh?

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.750
<b>Can you come to school early tomorrow?</b>

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.750
<b>there's something I want to give you</b>

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:10.210
<b>Come to school early tomorrow</b>

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:10.210
<b>and you might find something nice!</b>

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:15.420
<b>Is there anything that you want?</b>

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:22.380
<b>Can you meet up with me now?</b>

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.830
<b>Can you meet up with me now?</b>

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:31.580
Nishikata...

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.080
What a coincidence.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.290
Well, I saw your bike... stopped at the entrance.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:51.710
Oh.

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.380
S-so hey,

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:02.130
I actually got chocolate from some girls
in the grade under us today.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:08.170
Though it was just a mistake in the end. It wasn't really
for me, they had meant to give it to Shibasaki instead.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:14.710
I had been thinking about telling you about it,
but I couldn't really find a good time to... and so...

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:15.460
I already knew.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:16.790
Huh? Really?

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:17.460
Yep.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.630
Aw, jeez.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.500
It was kinda bumming me out the whole day.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:22.750
Same here.

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:26.540
I was feeling bummed the entire day, too.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:32.380
To be honest, I really didn't want to hear you say
anything about getting chocolates from those girls.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:38.460
I got the feeling I would start acting
mean again if you told me yourself.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:40.880
And I didn't want that to happen.

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:45.420
That's why everything was off today,
I couldn't tease you like usual.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:49.210
It kinda upset me that I had to be like that...

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.040
I'm sorry.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.790
No, I'm the one who's sorry!

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:00.750
I didn't mean to make you feel bad.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:05.960
Wait.

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:09.710
How did Takagi-san even know
that I got those chocolates?

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:11.420
Don't tell me...

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:12.960
Here, Nishikata.

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:20.170
The truth is, I was planning to put it
in your shoe locker this morning.

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.380
I considered just waiting until tomorrow,

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:26.670
but I really wanted to make sure
that you got it on February 14th.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.460
Will you accept it?

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:35.130
Th-thanks...

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:39.830
Can I open it?

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:45.000
Huh?

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.080
Dried sardines?

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:50.080
February 14th is national dried sardine day, remember?

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.460
Curse you, Takagi-san!

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:59.830
I was so happy when you brought up
dried sardine day, Nishikata.

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:02.380
I guess we've started to think alike, huh?

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:04.210
From all the time we spend together!

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.080
I'll save these to give to a cat.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:11.330
Here!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.580
This is my real gift for you, Nishikata.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.130
Thanks...

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.960
This is great. I got to give it to you on February 14th.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:22.540
Now my heart feels totally clear.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:28.040
Hey, let's try that eraser contest again tomorrow. Okay?

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:29.330
Oh, sure.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.460
Well, it's already clear that I'm gonna win.

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:33.420
You don't know that!

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.920
Darn you, Takagi-san!

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:45.080
Something the matter, Hamaguchi?

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:48.830
What's up? You said you wanted
to talk about something?

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:52.210
Oh boy, you finally gonna man up and say the "L" word?

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:53.000
That's right.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:53.830
Wha?!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.830
On White Day, I'm gonna tell Hojo that I love her.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:58.750
Whoa...

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:01.960
So listen, Nishikata...

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:05.210
You better tell Takagi-san that
you love her on that day, too!

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:06.460
Huh?

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.920
What?!
